## Why This Project Matters

- Addresses a **real, expensive industry pain**
- Demonstrates practical AI engineering, not hype
- Combines vision, language, and reasoning
- Bridges mechanical engineering and machine learning
- Enables faster retrofits and modernization

---

## Why This Project Is Personally Motivating

- Directly targets a frustrating manual workflow
- Uses domain expertise in HVAC and mechanical systems
- Produces visible, tangible outcomes
- Emphasizes systems thinking and explainability
- Balances automation with engineering judgment

---

## MVP Scope (Conference Demo)

- Input: PDF HVAC drawing + equipment schedule
- Output:
  - structured JSON of HVAC components
  - inferred connections with confidence scores
- Visualization outside Revit (optional)

A full Revit plugin is **not required** for initial impact.

---

## Future Extensions

- Revit API integration
- Semi-automated component placement
- Feedback-driven model improvement
- Support for other MEP systems (plumbing, electrical)

---

## Summary

This project demonstrates how AI can meaningfully reduce manual engineering labor by structuring messy real-world data, while respecting domain constraints and human expertise. It represents **practical, high-impact AI engineering** at the intersection of mechanical systems, multimodal learning, and real-world workflows.
